[0.025, "o", "\u001b[2mpotsherd ask \"what did we decide about prepared statements behind the pooler?\"\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n  We decided to disable client-side prepared statement caching by setting\r\n  statement_cache_size=0. \u001b[38;5;209m[1]\u001b[0m This was chosen because prepared\r\n  statements don't survive transaction boundaries under pgbouncer's transaction\r\n  pooling mode. \u001b[38;5;209m[1]\u001b[0m A test confirmed the decision: it failed\r\n  against the old client config with a \"prepared statement already exists\"\r\n  error, and passed once the cache was disabled. \u001b[38;5;209m[2]\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nEVIDENCE\r\n  [1] data-pipeline/9c4d2f18  21 aug 09:31  \u001b[2m\"The change here is one line eithe…\"\u001b[0m\r\n  [2] data-pipeline/9c4d2f18  21 aug 09:42  \u001b[2m\"Done. The test fails against the…\"\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nOPEN THREADS\r\n  \u001b[38;5;214mpossible open thread\u001b[0m · decided in event-bus, not seen in data-pi…\r\n      Configure consumers to connect to connection pooler on 6432 instead of\r\n      postgres on 5432\r\n      \u001b[2mevent-bus/b2181bfe@1,2  11 aug 11:38\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  6 of 53 sessi"]
